# 25. IMPLEMENTATION PRIORITY

When implementation begins, prioritize in this order:

### PHASE Q1 — CRYPTOGRAPHIC INVENTORY

Create a structured representation of cryptographic posture for selected infrastructure assets.

Goal:

The system knows WHAT cryptography an asset depends on.

---

### PHASE Q2 — QUANTUM EXPOSURE SCORE

Create an explainable deterministic scoring model.

Goal:

The system knows WHICH assets have the highest future quantum exposure and WHY.

---

### PHASE Q3 — GRAPH INTEGRATION

Map quantum exposure onto the existing city graph.

Goal:

The system understands that cryptographic exposure exists within dependencies rather than isolated assets.

---

### PHASE Q4 — VISUALIZATION

Add quantum-risk visualization to the existing graph.

Goal:

Judges can immediately SEE the difference between:

normal infrastructure

and

quantum-exposed infrastructure.

---

### PHASE Q5 — MIGRATION PRIORITIZATION

Generate prioritized migration recommendations.

Goal:

The platform becomes a decision-support system rather than merely a dashboard.

---

### PHASE Q6 — AI COMMANDER

Integrate quantum evidence into Commander assessments.

Goal:

The AI can explain:

"What is exposed?"

"Why?"

"What depends on it?"

"What should we prioritize?"

---

### PHASE Q7 — OPTIONAL PQC PROOF OF CONCEPT

Only if sufficient time remains:

Demonstrate a controlled PQC or hybrid cryptographic operation using an established implementation/library.

This is OPTIONAL.

Do not compromise the core project to achieve this.

